# SmartPBX Security Rules

Security is a first-class requirement.

Rules:

1. Never hardcode passwords, API keys or tokens.
2. Never commit .env files.
3. Validate all external input.
4. Authenticate all private API endpoints.
5. Authorize users based on roles and permissions.
6. Use API tokens for Python-to-Laravel communication.
7. Rate-limit sensitive endpoints where appropriate.
8. Do not expose Asterisk AMI publicly.
9. Restrict AMI access by IP/network.
10. Do not log passwords, API keys or authentication tokens.
11. Use HTTPS in production.
12. Sanitize user-controlled data.
13. Protect against SQL injection through framework/database abstractions.
14. Protect against XSS and CSRF where applicable.
15. Follow least-privilege principles.
16. Never disable security mechanisms just to make development easier without documenting it.
